      "message": "For the failure of the `emulator-linux_x64_nolocationui on aosp-emu-master-dev`, `emulator-linux_aarch64 on aosp-emu-master-dev`, and `sdk_tools_windows on aosp-emu-master-dev`. The flatbuffers\u0027 cmake version scripts fails to discover the correct version from git output.\n```\n... -- Proceeding with version: android-mainline-12.0.0_r122-823-gac8e08f7.android-mainline-12.0.0_r122-823-gac8e08f7.android-mainline-12.0.0_r122-823-gac8e08f7.android-mainline-12.0.0_r122-823-gac8e08f7\n21:37:56(00:16.75) bld | CMake Error at C:/buildbot/src/android/emu-master-dev/external/flatbuffers/CMakeLists.txt:23 (project):\n21:37:56(00:16.52) bld | VERSION\n21:37:56(00:16.52) bld | \"android-mainline-12.0.0_r122-823-gac8e08f7.android-mainline-12.0.0_r122-823-gac8e08f7.android-mainline-12.0.0_r122-823-gac8e08f7\"\n   \n```\n\nFor the `gfxstream_sdk_tools_linux on aosp-emu-master-dev` target, it fails because our cmake scripts to detect unlicensed targets are not working properly.\n\nTo fix the version issue, I am going to patch the flatbuffers\u0027 CMakeLists.txt to not to use the CMake script to detect the version. Unfortunately, we will diverge from the upstream, but I will work on a CL in the upstream to bypass the issue. We can revert this temporary patch then.\n\nFor the failure on scripts unable to detect unlicensed targets correctly, I am going to put up a CL in external/qemu on the `emu-master-dev` branch to fix this issue, and add that CL to this topic.",
